WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.703
Focus Tube turns YouTube videos and
playlists into a personal learning workspace.

00:00:04.703 --> 00:00:10.553
The idea is simple: keep the lesson, your
progress, notes, and next actions together.

00:00:10.553 --> 00:00:14.337
This tour uses sample accounts
and original demonstration media.

00:00:14.337 --> 00:00:20.865
YouTube discovery, playback, email, AI responses,
and extension connections are simulated.

00:00:20.865 --> 00:00:26.539
Account, planning, notebook, and feedback
changes use a disposable local database.

00:00:26.539 --> 00:00:30.656
Nothing here exposes a real learner's
account or spends money on a provider.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.384
New members join through an invitation.

00:00:34.384 --> 00:00:39.045
Opening the link removes its secret from the
visible address and keeps it in page memory.

00:00:39.045 --> 00:00:45.765
The account step asks for an email address, display
name, required username, and matching passwords.

00:00:45.765 --> 00:00:51.377
Username availability appears while typing, and
the server checks uniqueness again at registration.

00:00:51.377 --> 00:00:55.231
Password length and estimated strength
update from the first character.

00:00:55.231 --> 00:00:59.583
The eye buttons reveal either password
independently without changing its value.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:07.278
When optional analytics is enabled, About you asks for a
self-reported learning role, goal, and discovery source.

00:01:07.278 --> 00:01:10.863
Sharing is off by default, and skipping is a valid path.

00:01:10.863 --> 00:01:13.834
These answers are not inferred from social accounts.

00:01:13.834 --> 00:01:17.173
Next, the member enters a six-digit email code.

00:01:17.173 --> 00:01:21.292
This demo uses a simulated mail adapter, not a real inbox.

00:01:21.292 --> 00:01:24.106
Back and retry preserve the form where appropriate.

00:01:24.106 --> 00:01:28.967
Existing members can sign in with email
or username, without another invitation.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:33.735
For the rest of the tour, we switch
to a populated demo workspace.

00:01:33.735 --> 00:01:39.257
Grid and List show the same courses, including
lesson counts, duration, and completion.

00:01:39.257 --> 00:01:44.757
Pin useful courses and combine the Pinned filter
with Not started, In progress, or Completed.

00:01:44.757 --> 00:01:47.470
An empty filtered view offers Clear filters.

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:52.087
Removing a course is separate from opening
it, and does not delete its written notebook.

00:01:52.087 --> 00:01:56.766
The compact sidebar keeps navigation
available without consuming the whole screen.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:01.744
Search a topic, or paste a supported
YouTube video or playlist link.

00:02:01.744 --> 00:02:06.630
Keyword searches offer All, Videos,
Playlists, and Courses filters.

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:08.777
Typing alone does not send a search.

00:02:08.777 --> 00:02:14.102
Results show the creator, available duration,
and a preview when metadata provides one.

00:02:14.102 --> 00:02:19.452
Create course saves a result without leaving the
list, then changes its action to Open course.

00:02:19.452 --> 00:02:21.712
Direct links follow the import path.

00:02:21.712 --> 00:02:26.305
Refreshing a playlist can discover new
lessons while preserving existing progress.

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:36.215
The player provides play and pause, previous and next,
seeking, ten-second jumps, volume, mute, captions, quality, and

00:02:36.215 --> 00:02:36.759
fullscreen.

00:02:36.759 --> 00:02:39.056
Playback speed is remembered per course.

00:02:39.056 --> 00:02:45.182
Real YouTube embeds can clamp speed or override
quality, so a requested value is not a guarantee.

00:02:45.182 --> 00:02:46.993
Pausing lightly dims the frame.

00:02:46.993 --> 00:02:52.658
Controls hide when idle and remain accessible
through pointer, keyboard, and touch interaction.

00:02:52.658 --> 00:02:57.194
A first touch can reveal hidden controls
without unexpectedly pausing the lesson.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:04.014
Course content sits beside the player on a wide screen
and becomes a dismissible overlay on smaller screens.

00:03:04.014 --> 00:03:10.489
It combines the lesson list, completed status,
progress, time remaining, and a course checklist.

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:14.016
Chapters and description timestamps
jump to their source moments.

00:03:14.016 --> 00:03:20.069
You can mark a lesson complete manually; playback can
also drive completion and a next-lesson countdown.

00:03:20.069 --> 00:03:25.002
The important distinction is that opening a course
alone does not mean you started or completed it.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:28.003
Notes share the study area with the video.

00:03:28.003 --> 00:03:33.458
Choose Edit to write with headings,
emphasis, lists, links, and code formatting.

00:03:33.458 --> 00:03:39.151
Drag the divider or bottom grip to adjust the
writing area; keyboard resizing is also available.

00:03:39.151 --> 00:03:41.468
Notes autosave after a short pause.

00:03:41.468 --> 00:03:46.521
Saved means the server acknowledged the document,
not merely that text appeared on screen.

00:03:46.521 --> 00:03:50.072
Closing and reopening the pane
preserves the editor and its draft.

00:03:50.072 --> 00:03:54.724
In Read mode, source-linked paragraphs take
you back to the captured lesson moment.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:59.389
The Notebooks view brings written lessons
together without starting playback.

00:03:59.389 --> 00:04:02.374
Filter to one lesson or read the whole course notebook.

00:04:02.374 --> 00:04:09.058
Export Markdown creates a portable document, and Print
or Save PDF uses a clean print layout with source links.

00:04:09.058 --> 00:04:12.038
Removed courses can remain as archived notebooks.

00:04:12.038 --> 00:04:16.063
A failed save keeps a recovery draft
when browser storage is available.

00:04:16.063 --> 00:04:22.220
A conflicting edit presents an explicit choice between your
draft and the saved version rather than silently merging

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:23.246
or overwriting either.

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:26.452
Tasks turn a lesson into something actionable.

00:04:26.452 --> 00:04:31.813
Add a title, notes, priority, due
date, and optional course association.

00:04:31.813 --> 00:04:38.536
The quick panel lets you capture a task without leaving
your current screen, while the Tasks page offers course and

00:04:38.536 --> 00:04:39.209
priority filters.

00:04:39.209 --> 00:04:44.475
Roadmaps arrange courses into an ordered learning
path with combined progress and a Continue action.

00:04:44.475 --> 00:04:46.971
Course checklists stay close to their lessons.

00:04:46.971 --> 00:04:51.998
The global Board entry is marked Coming soon; it
is not a working board hidden behind this tour.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:57.134
The Dashboard separates time on Focus
Tube from recorded video watch time.

00:04:57.134 --> 00:05:04.816
It shows streaks, completed lessons and courses, daily
activity, course focus, consistency, and watch history.

00:05:04.816 --> 00:05:08.355
Change the time range to compare
recent learning with the longer view.

00:05:08.355 --> 00:05:12.369
Expand the data tables for an
accessible alternative to the charts.

00:05:12.369 --> 00:05:18.021
These are application activity records, not proof
that a person paid attention for every second.

00:05:18.021 --> 00:05:22.782
The values in this recording are demonstration
data, not real product analytics.

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:27.580
When configured by the operator,
Ask opens private video chat.

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:32.062
The first question requests permission to
process the video's content with Google.

00:05:32.062 --> 00:05:35.344
Available captions are prepared only after that choice.

00:05:35.344 --> 00:05:39.538
Summarize video and Explain the key
ideas are ordinary chat starters.

00:05:39.538 --> 00:05:42.894
Text appears provisionally while the response is processed.

00:05:42.894 --> 00:05:47.868
Only a validated completed answer gains
actionable source timestamps and note actions.

00:05:47.868 --> 00:05:55.109
This is caption-grounded assistance, not analysis of
unseen slides, code, or video frames, and citations do not

00:05:55.109 --> 00:05:57.665
guarantee that every claim is correct.

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:01.770
New chat starts a separate conversation for the same video.

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:07.780
Histories can be selected, renamed, or deleted,
and unsent drafts stay with their conversation.

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:10.354
Add to notes first opens an editable preview.

00:06:10.354 --> 00:06:16.939
Cancel writes nothing; Append to notes is the explicit
insertion step, with the normal save acknowledgement and

00:06:16.939 --> 00:06:17.714
immediate Undo.

00:06:17.714 --> 00:06:21.337
The composer displays the remaining
six-hour request allowance.

00:06:21.337 --> 00:06:24.505
That allowance is separate from the shared monthly AI budget.

00:06:24.505 --> 00:06:29.842
A refill does not reset spending, and stopping
an admitted request is not a refund promise.

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:38.162
Settings groups account details, password changes,
email verification, appearance, data, and policies.

00:06:38.162 --> 00:06:43.610
Sensitive changes require the current
password, and password changes rotate sessions.

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:50.596
Light and dark themes, optional navigation reflection,
and reduced transparency let the workspace adapt to your

00:06:50.596 --> 00:06:51.033
preferences.

00:06:51.033 --> 00:06:59.149
A learning backup includes your courses, planning, notes,
transcripts, and completed conversations, but not passwords,

00:06:59.149 --> 00:07:02.396
sessions, provider keys, or spending ledgers.

00:07:02.396 --> 00:07:07.106
Import replaces the current member's learning
data after validation and confirmation.

00:07:07.106 --> 00:07:10.447
It is not an administrator's full-instance database restore.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:17.415
Feedback opens as a separate page, so reporting a problem
does not need to replace your lesson or note draft.

00:07:17.415 --> 00:07:22.173
Choose a category, describe the issue,
and optionally attach screenshots.

00:07:22.173 --> 00:07:23.565
Private is the default.

00:07:23.565 --> 00:07:29.277
Public reports require explicit agreement
to publish the text, username, and images.

00:07:29.277 --> 00:07:31.873
Replies stay in the report's conversation.

00:07:31.873 --> 00:07:37.385
Image processing removes metadata, but it cannot
redact secrets visible in the picture itself.

00:07:37.385 --> 00:07:42.413
Forum version one does not automatically send
feedback email or publish a GitHub issue.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:48.842
An administrator can issue a reusable invitation
with a chosen successful-signup limit and expiry.

00:07:48.842 --> 00:07:54.677
Raw links are shown once; the issued list
contains metadata, status, and remaining uses.

00:07:54.677 --> 00:08:01.024
Expiry edits and revocation are guarded, and revoking an
invitation does not remove members who already joined.

00:08:01.024 --> 00:08:06.524
In Feedback, administrators can change
status, lock replies, or hide a thread.

00:08:06.524 --> 00:08:10.618
Resolved is not the same as locked,
and hidden is not the same as deleted.

00:08:10.618 --> 00:08:15.514
Administrator status does not grant access to
another member's private learning notebook.

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:21.690
Site monitoring gives administrators an
Overview, Members, Events, and System view.

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:28.472
Filter account metadata, inspect bounded activity events,
and check the application process and its storage.

00:08:28.472 --> 00:08:33.056
Presence is approximate, and the traffic
chart is not a permanent outage history.

00:08:33.056 --> 00:08:37.068
Optional product analytics is
separately configured and consent-based.

00:08:37.068 --> 00:08:44.182
It distinguishes engagement, retention, and self-reported
audience information, while withholding small groups.

00:08:44.182 --> 00:08:49.496
Enabling these screens in this disposable demo does
not enable collection on the real installation.

00:08:49.496 --> 00:08:54.508
External Grafana and uptime integrations
also require operator configuration.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:09:02.118
The optional desktop browser extension captures one supported
YouTube video through its popup or context-menu action.

00:09:02.118 --> 00:09:07.411
This scene shows the real popup interface with
simulated browser connection and save receipts.

00:09:07.411 --> 00:09:13.109
Choose one destination, grant its site
permission, connect the current profile, and save.

00:09:13.109 --> 00:09:17.153
Already-saved videos return a receipt
instead of a duplicate course.

00:09:17.153 --> 00:09:20.413
Pending operations offer manual Retry or Discard.

00:09:20.413 --> 00:09:27.318
The extension does not read browsing history, import a
whole playlist, or give mobile browsers the same extension

00:09:27.318 --> 00:09:27.702
capability.

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:32.218
A completed course unlocks the application's PDF certificate.

00:09:32.218 --> 00:09:36.452
It records completion inside Focus
Tube; it is not accreditation.

00:09:36.452 --> 00:09:42.583
The core experience is the loop from discovery to
watching, writing, asking, planning, and reviewing.

00:09:42.583 --> 00:09:44.874
Manual notes need no AI service.

00:09:44.874 --> 00:09:49.431
Optional backend media downloads require
separate tools and appropriate rights.

00:09:49.431 --> 00:09:56.087
Social sign-in, the Board interface, and the proposed motion
improvements are not demonstrated as shipped features.

00:09:56.087 --> 00:10:02.372
Newer uncommitted cache work is discussed in the architecture
video, separately from this released demo baseline.
